<h2><span class="n">PART 2</span> The Shadow Desk &amp; Promotion</h2>

<p class="lead">This section was built from scratch on this week's numbers &mdash; no gate, candidate or verdict was inherited from last week's report. I ranked the whole shadow board on honest tick-repriced dollars (what a trade would really have made after slippage and fees, never the optimistic sim price), and let the promotion pick fall out of that ranking rather than deciding it in advance. Then I ran the full robustness battery on whatever came top, presented the two grind-exit shadow ledgers exactly as they stand tonight, and re-proved the exit ladder on the week's tick path per regime. Where the sample is thin I say so plainly &mdash; the shadow board <em>nominates</em>, the paper desk <em>judges</em>.</p>

<div class="card">
<h3>The shadow board, ranked on honest money</h3>
<p>Every strategy that runs observe-only alongside the live desk, sorted by real (tick-repriced) dollars. Two windows: all-time (the ~two-week summer archive, 07-16 to 07-31) and this week. The green rows are the ones actually making money on honest fills; the red block at the bottom is where the dead ideas live.</p>

